00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:18.720
MILLION COLOR!

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:20.180
TURNS!

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:26.640
<i>It's not an easy thing to navigate from the Moon to the Earth, but...</i>

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:30.650
<i>...the taboo from the past was what made this especially challenging.</i>

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:34.740
<i>The Whales soon touched ground in North Ameria...</i>

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:38.740
<i>...Because Queen Dianna desires to quickly put an end to this situation.</i>

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:44.330
<i>And now for that very purpose, she attempted to reason with Sir Guin and Merrybell.</i>

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:53.710
<b>Dianna's Repatriation</b>

00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:14.440
What's the big deal with this Moonlight Butterfly system?

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:15.860
Watch this!

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:21.030
It's coming this way...

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:22.830
It's pretty big, isn't it?

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:33.460
It may not be perfect, but we should be able to use this as a pretty effective weapon!

00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:45.930
I'm not sure what they're doing, but I know the meaning of this typhoon...

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:51.060
And that ionic smell...

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:54.360
- I'll be back soon!
- Okay.

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:02.950
Yo, nobleman's son. What's up?

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:07.240
They've gone too far, now! This earth isn't a laboratory...

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:10.040
In war, there is no upper limit for such actions.

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:14.540
These are the letters from the leaders in Ameria who'll be forming a resistance.

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:19.760
They say that they have no intentions of participating in our plan to unify and reconstruct this nation.

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:25.350
Personally, I have no interest in the unification of the population and continent of Ameria.

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:28.850
Even Inglessa has a limit on how many resources it can supply us with, you know.

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:30.940
That could be a problem.

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:32.650
Then perhaps...

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:34.150
What?

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:36.650
Shall we shift our focus onto Dianna Counter?

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:40.530
Are you suggesting that we start cannibalizing our own?

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:43.860
You won't have to take it that far.

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:47.530
With the power of the Turn X, it should be quite easy to defeat the Dianna Counter forces.

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:52.750
Once Phil and the other leaders see it for themselves, they'll be more than willing to bow to such pure power.

00:03:55.630 --> 00:04:00.050
Phil's army has been something of a thorn. Shall we attack?

00:04:00.050 --> 00:04:03.550
Yes. Then, could you return the Turn A to us?

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:06.430
Are you saying you don't trust us with it?

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:11.640
It's not that. The technicians won't stop pestering me about it until I allow them to begin the mass production of the unit.

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:14.140
Mass production of the Turn A...

00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:17.560
- Sounds interesting, doesn't it?
- Yes, very interesting.

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:28.740
Please don't do something so unreasonable, Joseph!

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:30.740
That's right, please consider the current situation!

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:34.750
If you head to meet with Guin alone, you'll get yourself killed!

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:37.330
As things are now, there's nothing that Loran can possibly accomplish!

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:40.960
Because of that, I need to take the Jalopy team and recover the unit!

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:43.840
But negotiations with Dianna Counter's forces are going smoothly!

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:45.840
This isn't the time for you to such things!

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:49.050
And how do you know we can trust these negotiations with the Moonrace?

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:50.760
The Militia leadership needs to be handled...

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:52.140
You're just being prejudice!

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:56.730
The Moonrace has even less desire to damage Earth than the people of Earth do!

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:59.060
It's where we want to live!

00:04:59.060 --> 00:05:01.440
What the little sister said is precisely right!

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:05.240
Isn't our Queen be with the Almaiya class ship that arrived here?

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:09.740
Watch that tone! If you're part of the Moonrace, what in blazes are you wearing!?

00:05:09.740 --> 00:05:14.460
It's no stranger than Terrans like you using a Mobile Suit, I'd say.

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:17.120
I suppose you won't be guiding my way.

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:18.630
Who was that?

00:05:18.630 --> 00:05:21.840
That voice sounds familiar... could he be a Moonrace spy?

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:23.340
I have no idea...

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:28.930
Look, FLAT boy, I can get there on my own. You don't need to follow me.

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:32.140
Whales, can you hear me? There's a spy on the way.

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:35.430
Hey, what's your name? I'll tell them to expect you.

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:38.560
It's Corin! I'm Sergeant Corin Nander.

00:05:42.730 --> 00:05:44.740
Corin's here!?

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:46.740
That monk is...

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:52.450
I hope you're currently in good health, Highness.

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:56.960
I appreciate your concern, Sergeant Corin.

00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:00.130
Wasn't he the pilot of that strange Mechanical Doll?

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:05.460
That's right... He dedicated his efforts to Dianna. That's the guy who kept calling the White Doll "Gundam".

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:11.260
I just recently began to smell that apocalyptic ionic stench.

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:13.930
Then I take it that you've seen the Turn A in action?

00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:15.560
Yes, I have.

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:19.140
Your majesty, what I have witnessed...

00:06:19.140 --> 00:06:22.560
...Was only a fraction of the horrors that machine is capable of.

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:25.650
Then just who exactly is this man?

00:06:25.650 --> 00:06:30.160
I myself am only aware of the records contained within Dianna Counter.

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:36.040
But Corin here predates all of them. So I can't tell you anything for sure.

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:40.040
Naturally, I can't blame your majesty for neglecting to learn such things.

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:44.750
Sergeant Corin... do you know of a way that we might be able to combat the Turn A?

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:48.050
Sadly, my existence won't be that convenient.

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:49.430
But...

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:55.060
Once I awakened, I got the opportunity to see our young highness all grown up.

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:58.430
I'll help you in any way I can if it would give me a chance to be near you.

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:03.940
Sergeant Corin, I would like to officially request you to join my forces.

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:05.230
Yes!

00:07:05.230 --> 00:07:07.730
Thank you for everything.

00:07:07.730 --> 00:07:10.450
It is my pleasure, Corin.

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:17.040
So.. could this be the behavior of a person sent into prolonged hibernation?

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:19.830
Mr. Corin...

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:24.540
A samurai who has hibernated for ages...

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:33.140
Joseph, please wait!

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:37.060
If you go to Guin Rhineford alone, you'll get yourself captured, or worse!

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:40.230
I'll be with the Jalopy team, so don't worry about it.

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:42.060
Loran, stop him!

00:07:42.060 --> 00:07:44.730
Joseph seems to think that he'll be able to recapture Turn A!

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:47.020
Stop his team from heading out!

00:07:47.020 --> 00:07:49.440
I'll go directly to Guin and see what his true intentions are!

00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:55.530
I'm heading out in the Core Fighter!
- I am too!

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:57.160
- I'll help them.
- We'll leave it to you.

00:07:57.160 --> 00:07:59.750
Sochie, Miashei, do whatever you can to stop them!

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:07.340
Joseph is a man with great potential! Please stop him from doing anything reckless!

00:08:07.340 --> 00:08:09.250
- We're flying...
- It'll be just fine.

00:08:09.250 --> 00:08:12.550
What a messy situation...

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:14.930
How can an army like this possibly hope to win?

00:08:14.930 --> 00:08:18.260
Especially when those bastards are using a Gundam...

00:08:18.260 --> 00:08:21.640
This is why I've re-enlisted you in our forces, Sergeant.

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:24.650
If you wish it, The Royal Guard will loan you a unit.

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:26.150
A SUMO, huh?

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:33.860
That's the signal to begin this battle...

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:37.950
But since I'm such a nice guy, I'll give you a chance to prepare first!

00:08:39.330 --> 00:08:41.160
Sweatson Sutero?

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:43.830
That will be the mercy of the Ghingnham Squad!

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:46.330
So this is the end result of Agrippa's demise?

00:08:46.330 --> 00:08:47.830
Commander Phil!

00:08:47.830 --> 00:08:51.460
We can handle the Mahiroo. The WaDoms can destroy them in a single blast.

00:08:51.460 --> 00:08:55.760
Don't think I'll let you surrender just because you're a voluntary civilian force.

00:08:56.760 --> 00:08:58.140
Ghingnham Squadron...

00:08:58.140 --> 00:09:01.060
Your actions on Earth constitute a serious war crime, yet you seem to take pride in them!

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:05.230
If these orders came from General Ghingnham himself...

00:09:05.230 --> 00:09:08.440
...then his sentence in the eyes of the Dianna Counter's laws is very clear.

00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:11.730
I'll handle their Aspite for you.

00:09:11.730 --> 00:09:13.740
- Please do.
- Yes sir.

00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:15.450
Prepare the barrier!

00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:16.950
You've been warned!

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:25.750
WaDom, commence the attack!

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:36.550
So Phil wants to become the ruler of the Soleil Kingdom in the middle of Nocis? I can't allow that!

00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:41.050
Then again, I might let you live if you build a delicious cake shop in it!

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:48.560
Nocis is going to become a battlefield...

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:50.650
We'll have to force the Soleil out.

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:53.530
You sure it's okay for us to travel to the factories at a time like this?

00:09:53.530 --> 00:09:57.530
The technicians need to be given the opportunity to examine the Turn A.

00:09:57.740 --> 00:10:02.660
That way, it won't matter anymore if that one little lady attempts to take back Turn A.

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:04.540
Is that our purpose, then?

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:07.750
What makes you think Ghingnham will loan us the Turn A again?

00:10:07.750 --> 00:10:11.750
Well, he believes anyone who isn't of the Moonrace can't pilot it.

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:15.050
Yeah. Loran isn't here with us now.

00:10:15.050 --> 00:10:17.340
Neither Loran or Laura...

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:22.760
Why must the Moonrace battle their own?

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:26.730
The Terrans have been known to war among themselves time and time again. It's nothing unexpected.

00:10:26.930 --> 00:10:28.850
But... Queen Dianna...

00:10:28.850 --> 00:10:30.650
The Whales must leave at once.

00:10:30.650 --> 00:10:31.360
Right!

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:32.650
Queen Dianna!

00:10:32.650 --> 00:10:35.860
Sooner or later, Phil and the Soleil will be set upon.

00:10:35.860 --> 00:10:38.150
But we too must now set off.

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:41.030
With our assistance, they should be able to fend off the Ghingnham team.

00:10:41.030 --> 00:10:43.240
But Phil and Ambassador Miran are...

00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:47.250
You were once the sole commander of the Soleil.

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:51.250
So you should know better than anyone that they're not bad people.

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:53.630
That's true.

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:56.340
They will welcome our response.

00:10:56.340 --> 00:11:00.840
Harry, ask Captain Daisuke to take command of the Whales and then determine our course.

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:01.760
Ma'am!

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:04.350
I would also like to see Sergeant Corin once again.

00:11:06.850 --> 00:11:09.640
We are soon going to pay a visit to Guin Rhineford.

00:11:09.640 --> 00:11:12.850
For this purpose, the Jalopy Team will coordinate with Whales' forces!

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:19.860
However, the people of earth won't merely be the Moonrace's subordinates. They can't just use us to bulk up their forces!

00:11:19.860 --> 00:11:23.660
- We'll follow any order given!
- Shall we launch early morning?

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:25.950
All of you, be sure to rest well!

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:33.960
I told you to work without the lights!

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:37.250
Do we know what the Willgem's course currently is?

00:11:37.250 --> 00:11:40.340
Yes... but confronting Mr. Guin will only prove a useless effort.

00:11:40.340 --> 00:11:42.630
Do you really believe that I'd bet our efforts on a simple chat?

00:11:42.630 --> 00:11:44.260
What do you mean?

00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:47.430
I'll show you how an underpowered team learns to fight.

00:11:47.430 --> 00:11:49.060
Then I'm going too.

00:11:49.060 --> 00:11:50.730
I'm going as well.

00:11:50.730 --> 00:11:52.060
I'm going too!

00:11:56.860 --> 00:11:57.650
Loran!

00:11:57.650 --> 00:11:59.280
This thing isn't capable of long distance flights.

00:12:16.710 --> 00:12:17.630
Power down the alarm...

00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:18.920
Docking request received!

00:12:18.920 --> 00:12:19.710
What is it?

00:12:19.710 --> 00:12:21.300
Open our Mobile Suit deck!

00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:30.100
- Loran has returned...
- That FLAT's from the Jalopy Team, right?

00:12:30.100 --> 00:12:32.390
Isn't it a bit late for you to reach us now?

00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:35.730
Why didn't you respond to the radio communications?

00:12:35.730 --> 00:12:37.610
Is it true that you made it to the moon?

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:39.110
What about it?

00:12:39.110 --> 00:12:42.900
Well, I'd love to see the hometown of my lady friend here someday.

00:12:44.320 --> 00:12:48.330
Does this mean you've decided to assist us, Laura?

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:49.700
Answer him.

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:53.500
I... just came to escort Joseph.

00:12:53.500 --> 00:12:55.920
Mr. Joseph Yaht?

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:59.500
Why have you decided to join forces with Gym Ghingnham?

00:12:59.500 --> 00:13:02.800
The Ghingnham Armada greatly outperforms this lone ship.

00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:09.430
In reality, what have we actually gained from our negotiations with the Moonrace?

00:13:09.430 --> 00:13:10.510
What?

00:13:10.510 --> 00:13:16.900
His own fleet would simply descend from the moon and wipe us out, along with the peace loving factions of the Moonrace.

00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:22.400
You are quite mistaken. Gym Ghingnham's faction alone would've never invaded earth without outside help.

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:26.320
Do you remember what you saw on the moon, Fran Doll?

00:13:26.320 --> 00:13:33.120
Ghingnham went around playing his war games even after the return operation began, didn't he?

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:37.120
You're referring to the Moonrace members whose fighting instinct resurfaced?

00:13:37.120 --> 00:13:38.790
That's right.

00:13:38.790 --> 00:13:43.420
And so, because of this, we have decided to ally ourselves with those samurai.

00:13:43.420 --> 00:13:48.720
That's only a good idea if you'll be able to keep Ghingnham as an ally, Sir Guin.

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:53.010
War is about more than just weapons.

00:13:53.010 --> 00:13:59.230
Education, industry, and even culture itself...These are all things which your opponent can sabotage.

00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:05.400
And so it has been to this end, that I sought to confront our enemies beforehand.

00:14:05.400 --> 00:14:07.030
We understand, Lord.

00:14:07.030 --> 00:14:11.030
I sought to accomplish great things here, but you ruined it by bringing that man to Earth!

00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:12.410
Is this kind of ambition a bad thing?

00:14:12.410 --> 00:14:13.490
What!?

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:17.000
To accomplish that, you just need to think like Ghingnham.

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:20.420
If we can mass produce the Turn A...

00:14:20.420 --> 00:14:23.630
...it wouldn't be much trouble to place someone like yourself in command of such a force.

00:14:23.630 --> 00:14:25.800
You mustn't! You can't accept this man's offer...

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:28.590
Someone of the Moonrace should stay out of this!

00:14:28.590 --> 00:14:33.430
So to help you control your alliance with Ghingnham, you want me to become your ally as well?

00:14:36.390 --> 00:14:37.730
That's not it.

00:14:37.730 --> 00:14:42.230
I'm simply asking an ambitious person like you if you'd be interested in that opportunity.

00:14:42.230 --> 00:14:44.020
We're both from earth, are we not?

00:14:44.610 --> 00:14:45.610
- It smells like smoke!
- A fire broke out!

00:14:45.610 --> 00:14:46.530
What?

00:14:46.530 --> 00:14:47.820
- Where's the extinguisher!?
- The alarms didn't go off!

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:50.110
Where have Bruno and Jacop gone!?

00:14:50.110 --> 00:14:52.200
They weren't on duty, were they?

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:55.490
It looks like even those two decided to flee from you.

00:14:55.490 --> 00:14:57.620
Seems like you're not too popular anymore.

00:14:57.620 --> 00:14:58.500
What?

00:14:58.500 --> 00:15:00.710
Here's my answer!

00:15:04.790 --> 00:15:06.300
- A blast?
- The emergency exit...

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:09.010
This probably won't be a good place for us to stay...

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:11.510
Then let's hurry up and get out of here!

00:15:12.090 --> 00:15:13.720
We need to escape before the smoke overtakes us...

00:15:14.430 --> 00:15:16.930
Just be grateful that we didn't use more powerful gunpowder!

00:15:17.430 --> 00:15:20.310
Couldn't you please reconsider the possibility of joining with Queen Dianna again?

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:22.600
That would make us become Ghingnham's enemy!

00:15:23.310 --> 00:15:25.900
Laura, why do you refuse to even consider assisting me!?

00:15:25.900 --> 00:15:28.030
I... I am...

00:15:30.400 --> 00:15:32.030
Laura!

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:34.410
We're searching for where the blast came from...

00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:36.200
Make sure you disable Joseph's FLAT!

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:37.990
Mr. Jacop!

00:15:37.990 --> 00:15:39.620
Did you hear the explosions?

00:15:39.620 --> 00:15:41.500
Did they hit our engine?

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:43.790
Give us a minute and we'll check it over...

00:15:45.500 --> 00:15:46.920
Loran, please take care of Fran.

00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:48.000
What about you, Joseph?

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:49.920
Got that? Just stick with Loran.

00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:51.720
- Joseph!
- Fran...

00:16:04.520 --> 00:16:06.900
The Soleil will now take a 180 degree course change in it's heading!

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:10.030
Watch our rear as we turn to face the opposing ship!

00:16:26.210 --> 00:16:29.300
Poe, the Mobile Suit unit will follow the planned operation...

00:16:29.300 --> 00:16:33.010
Roger! We'll show these guys what officers with real combat experience can do!

00:16:33.510 --> 00:16:35.590
SUMO-1 and WaDom-2, preparing for the combat operation!

00:16:36.220 --> 00:16:41.020
As you work with our lead ship, get ready to wipe out Ghingnham's soldiers in a single blow!

00:16:41.600 --> 00:16:43.230
Cease radio communication...

00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:45.230
Our opponents aren't the militia!

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:49.320
Carefully monitor their warship and look for an opening!

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:53.110
Oh, Mr. Loran, have you come here to take back the White Doll?

00:16:53.110 --> 00:16:54.530
Uh, may I?

00:16:56.320 --> 00:16:58.200
We're leaving, Loran! Mr. Joseph!

00:17:06.330 --> 00:17:07.630
Mr. Joseph!

00:17:09.130 --> 00:17:10.630
Joseph, get up there!

00:17:10.630 --> 00:17:12.010
I'm just fine.

00:17:12.010 --> 00:17:15.510
There's still a Borjarnon here...! Let's escape!

00:17:16.510 --> 00:17:18.010
- Hurry up!
- We'll take the exit to the right.

00:17:21.220 --> 00:17:22.430
I'll shoot!

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:49.420
Ready the main cannons!

00:17:49.920 --> 00:17:52.630
Adapt to whatever the battle throws your way. I'll leave it to you.

00:17:52.630 --> 00:17:54.800
Yes sir! You can count on me.

00:18:18.320 --> 00:18:20.910
They're attacking us from below instead of above?

00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:23.410
Miran, that bastard... He's pressuring us from all directions!

00:18:23.910 --> 00:18:25.910
Stay in the air! Prepare to engage the enemy battleship!

00:18:26.500 --> 00:18:28.410
Are you even watching this? Lower your altitude!

00:18:29.210 --> 00:18:33.500
The attack from below's meant to lure us away. Their real force will approach us from behind.

00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:35.420
Don't ascend, Number four!

00:18:36.010 --> 00:18:37.920
Gym, should I assist us in my Bandit?

00:18:40.010 --> 00:18:42.100
The first robotic warship has been sent in.

00:18:42.100 --> 00:18:43.720
So it would seem.

00:18:43.720 --> 00:18:45.520
Do you think we can sink two of them?

00:18:45.520 --> 00:18:47.020
I'm betting on three.

00:19:12.920 --> 00:19:16.420
Corin, it looks like the Mobile Suit combat has begun.

00:19:16.420 --> 00:19:17.630
Yes...

00:19:17.630 --> 00:19:20.430
Will you be able to get me to the Soleil in the midst of that?

00:19:20.430 --> 00:19:23.300
We'll make it.

00:19:28.310 --> 00:19:30.100
SUMO units, ready to deploy!

00:19:30.520 --> 00:19:32.020
The enemy's reinforcements have entered our firing range!

00:19:32.730 --> 00:19:33.610
Here they come!

00:19:34.730 --> 00:19:35.820
Fire!

00:19:42.820 --> 00:19:44.120
What's with that!?

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:46.490
The Bandits would've been able to take care of them much more easily...

00:19:46.490 --> 00:19:47.830
Pull us back!

00:19:47.830 --> 00:19:51.330
We'll bombard Harry while the Mahiroo Squadron forms a defensive line for us!

00:19:51.920 --> 00:19:53.790
Did earth's air eat away at your sanity?

00:20:01.130 --> 00:20:04.090
At this sort of range, being hit by even a single blast could prove deadly!

00:20:04.090 --> 00:20:05.430
Pull us out of here, now!

00:20:10.390 --> 00:20:11.230
Here they come!

00:20:13.730 --> 00:20:15.810
The Mahiroo are retreating?

00:20:46.720 --> 00:20:49.310
Why would that pesky mosquito be flying here?

00:20:49.310 --> 00:20:50.600
Wait, that's...

00:20:53.520 --> 00:20:55.310
That person...

00:20:57.900 --> 00:20:59.610
That person is...!

00:21:03.530 --> 00:21:05.200
Queen Dianna!

00:21:06.320 --> 00:21:08.030
Inform all personnel!

00:21:08.620 --> 00:21:10.330
That fighter plane is...

00:21:13.120 --> 00:21:17.630
All personnel, form up! Remove your headgear!

00:21:29.300 --> 00:21:33.220
l, Sergeant Corin, the former commander of the Zenoa Team...

00:21:33.220 --> 00:21:36.390
...have safely delivered Her Majesty, Dianna Soriel back to us.

00:21:37.230 --> 00:21:38.600
Commander Phil...

00:21:38.600 --> 00:21:41.900
...Gym Ghingnham has now reached the Earth.

00:21:41.900 --> 00:21:45.820
This too, is another sin I've allowed to occur.

00:21:46.900 --> 00:21:51.910
In order to strike against him, I will be in need of your service. As well as yours, Miran.

00:21:51.910 --> 00:21:53.910
Dianna Soriel, your Highness...

00:21:53.910 --> 00:21:56.000
My life is in your hands.

00:21:56.000 --> 00:22:03.630
I too intend to willingly follow any order that you will give me, your majesty.

00:22:03.630 --> 00:22:09.300
I now order the Dianna Counter forces to take whatever measures are necessary to strike down Ghingnham's Armada.

00:22:11.010 --> 00:22:11.930
Yes Ma'am!

00:22:30.870 --> 00:22:37.540
<b><i>Yama no ha tsuki wa michi</i></b>

00:22:30.870 --> 00:22:37.540
<b>As the full moon, casts itself over the mountain's edge...</b>

00:22:37.540 --> 00:22:44.590
<b><i>iki zuku anata no mori</i></b>

00:22:37.540 --> 00:22:44.590
<b>...it spreads the breath of life spreads into the forest where you stand...</b>

00:22:44.590 --> 00:22:51.720
<b><i>Natsu kusa abite nemuru</i></b>

00:22:44.590 --> 00:22:51.720
<b>As you sleep in the summer grass...</b>

00:22:51.760 --> 00:22:58.600
<b><i>Itooshii yokogao</i></b>

00:22:51.760 --> 00:22:58.600
<b>...your profile is a lovely sight to behold.</b>

00:23:00.850 --> 00:23:06.690
<b><i>Kaze ni</i></b>

00:23:00.850 --> 00:23:06.690
<b>The wind...</b>

00:23:06.690 --> 00:23:13.780
<b><i>LaLaLu... LaLaLu...</i></b>

00:23:13.780 --> 00:23:20.670
<b><i>utae... hane ni</i></b>

00:23:13.780 --> 00:23:20.670
<b>The sight of your wings, is seen...</b>

00:23:20.670 --> 00:23:25.170
<b><i>tsuki utsushi</i></b>

00:23:20.670 --> 00:23:25.170
<b>...in the moon's reflection.</b>

00:23:25.170 --> 00:23:32.800
<b><i>Inochi kagaya kase yo</i></b>

00:23:25.170 --> 00:23:32.800
<b>This wonderful life will shine vividly.</b>

00:23:40.390 --> 00:23:44.810
<i>Ghingnham begins utilizing the Turn X in his ground campaign.</i>

00:23:44.810 --> 00:23:47.110
<i>Joseph seems ready to risk his life...</i>

00:23:47.110 --> 00:23:50.820
<i>...and Lieutenant Harry and Dianna Counter are willing to risk theirs as well.</i>

00:23:50.820 --> 00:23:54.700
<i>After being watched by Queen Dianna, I've come to believe...</i>

00:23:54.700 --> 00:23:56.700
<i>...that I'll soon be flying into the light.</i>

00:23:59.410 --> 00:24:03.000
<i>Next time... on </i>TURN A GUNDAM...<i>
Moonlight Butterfly</i>

00:24:03.000 --> 00:24:05.290
"The wind turns violent."

00:24:03.500 --> 00:24:08.460
<b>Moonlight Butterfly</b>
